# /etc/inittab - services init starts at boot, one path per line.
#
# Read by userspace/init/main.c. Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
# Order matters only in that the GUI comes up before the shell.
#
# This file is the whole boot policy. The kernel has no list of programs and
# init has none compiled in: removing a line here is how a service stops
# starting, and no rebuild of anything is needed.
#
# Names are 8.3 because the FAT driver reads short directory entries and skips
# long-name (LFN) ones - "phone_daemon" would be stored under a mangled
# "PHONE_~1" short name and never found. Keep each component <= 8 characters.

/bin/gui
/bin/shell

# Modem backend - talks to /dev/uart1.
/bin/phoned

# FAT-write backend - keeps slow SD writes off the GUI task.
/bin/storaged
